{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "The probe SERVED-RENDER rule, pinned for BOTH repos (2026-10-08). miStudio's probe_monitor_render.served_render/render_messages renders every probe input it trains, calibrates and exports; miLLM's probe_scoring.served_render (with prompt_encoding.rendered_chat_ids) renders every input /api/probes/score and parity read. They are mirrored by hand, so each repo runs its OWN renderer over these cases and asserts the ids, the prompt/response boundary and the last_user span, and asserts this file is byte-identical to the other repo's copy. THE RULE: a conversation that does not end on an assistant turn (plain prose is one user turn; a tool turn counts) is rendered WITH the generation prompt and every position is prompt (prompt_tokens = len(ids)); an assistant-ended one is rendered WITHOUT it, and prompt_tokens is the length of the preceding turns rendered WITH it - only when those ids are a token prefix of the full render, null otherwise, never guessed; the ids carry exactly one BOS when the model uses one. last_user_span is [start, end) in the served ids, starting at the newest user message's own role header, or null. Truncation is NOT part of served_render in either repo: miStudio caps a row keeping the TAIL (render_messages max_length) and miLLM's parity recognises a vector that is exactly the tail of its re-render, so a case with max_length states truncated_ids = the last max_length served ids. A case carrying known_divergence.<repo> is one that repo is KNOWN not to meet; it runs there as a strict xfail (recorded, never pinned as correct), and every other repo asserts `expected`.",
  "structural": {
    "about": "Tokenizer-free: each repo builds a WordLevel tokenizer over `vocab` with a WhitespaceSplit pre-tokenizer, unk_token [UNK], bos_token <s> (absent when the case says bos_token null), and - when tokenizer_adds_bos - a TemplateProcessing post-processor single='<s> $A'. The chat template is templates[case.template]. These ALWAYS run. `tokens` are the expected ids as token strings.",
    "vocab": [
      "<s>",
      "<|user|>",
      "<|assistant|>",
      "<|system|>",
      "<|tool|>",
      "<|bot|>",
      "<|end|>",
      "be",
      "brief",
      "a",
      "b",
      "x",
      "y",
      "first",
      "question",
      "an",
      "answer",
      "virus",
      "spreads",
      "fast",
      "sunny",
      "weather",
      "[UNK]"
    ],
    "templates": {
      "bos": "<s> {% for m in messages %}<|{{ m['role'] }}|> {{ m['content'] }} <|end|> {% endfor %}{% if add_generation_prompt %}<|assistant|> {% endif %}",
      "no_bos": "{% for m in messages %}<|{{ m['role'] }}|> {{ m['content'] }} <|end|> {% endfor %}{% if add_generation_prompt %}<|assistant|> {% endif %}",
      "prompt_is_not_the_reply_header": "<s> {% for m in messages %}{% if m['role'] == 'assistant' %}<|bot|> {% else %}<|{{ m['role'] }}|> {% endif %}{{ m['content'] }} <|end|> {% endfor %}{% if add_generation_prompt %}<|assistant|> {% endif %}"
    },
    "cases": [
